Source: mangowm
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ackerman-00 <noreply@example.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), meson, ninja-build, pkg-config,
 libwayland-dev, libwayland-bin, wayland-protocols, libinput-dev,
 libxkbcommon-dev, libdrm-dev, libpcre2-dev, libpixman-1-dev,
 libcjson-dev, libpango1.0-dev, libcairo2-dev, libxcb1-dev,
 libxcb-icccm4-dev, libxcb-randr0-dev,
 libwlroots-0.20-dev (>= 0.20), libscenefx-0.5-dev (>= 0.5)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/mangowm/mango

Package: mangowm
Architecture: amd64
# wlroots + scenefx come from the OFFICIAL Debian packages in both
# supported suites (libwlroots-0.20 + libwlroots-0.20-dev,
# libscenefx-0.5 + libscenefx-0.5-dev, 0.20.2-1 / 0.5+ds-1). Stated
# explicitly so the mapping never depends on shlibs inference alone.
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
 libwlroots-0.20 (>= 0.20), libscenefx-0.5 (>= 0.5)
Description: Practical and powerful Wayland compositor (dwm-like)
 Mango is a fast, feature-rich Wayland compositor built on dwl,
 wlroots and scenefx: scrollable tiling, tags, animations, effects.
